  "qualified": "Engine differences the probe records instead of failing; each still holds its WebKit value. observerOrder: the order between observers in one update. WebKit (Document::updateIntersectionObservers) delivers in the order observers gained their first target and moves an observer that lost all its targets to the end when it observes again; Chromium 156's order varies between updates. rootBounds: with a scrollMargin, WebKit reports the root bounds of a document or implicit root grown by the scroll margin, while Chromium reports them without it; both clip by the grown scrollport, so isIntersecting, the intersection rectangle and the ratio agree. elementRootScrollMargin: with an explicit root (the document here), WebKit clips targets by the scroll containers between target and root without the scroll margin (IntersectionObserver::computeIntersectionState passes no scrollMargin when root() is set), so #v, clipped 10px below #c, is not intersecting; Chromium grows those scrollports and reports it at 0.2. The recorded WebKit entries are asserted.",
  "measured": {
    "time": "entry times lie within rv_host_now read before and after the rendering update that queued them and never decrease; rv_host_now is whole milliseconds and keeps its origin over rv_host_load_html; one frozen time per update",
    "takeRecords": "empty outside delivery in both engines; inside the first delivering callback the other observer entries are taken and its callback does not run",
    "teardown": "a target retained from an entry outlives removal and observer release; a released target is collected with no queued records; an observer of a replaced document never delivers; release inside a callback; host destroy"
  },
